From: CrispStrobe <cze+github@mailbox.org>
Subject: Fix XCHD A,@Ri and MOV direct,@Ri opcode bugs

Two opcode bugs found by systematic testing of all addressing modes.

1. XCHD A,@Ri (0xD6/0xD7): The low nibble exchange reads the already-
   modified ACC instead of saving the original value first. The memory
   byte's low nibble ends up as a copy of the new ACC low nibble, not
   the old one. Fix: save ACC & 0x0F before overwriting ACC.

   MCS-51 spec: "Exchanges the low-order nibble of the Accumulator
   (bits 3-0) with that of the internal RAM location indirectly
   addressed by the specified register."

   Test: A=0x34, @R0=0x12. Expected: A=0x32, @R0=0x14.
   Before fix: A=0x32, @R0=0x12 (nibble not exchanged).

2. MOV direct,@Ri (0x86/0x87): Source and destination are swapped.
   The code reads from OPERAND1 (the direct address) and writes to
   INDIR_RX_ADDRESS (@Ri), when it should do the opposite.

   MCS-51 spec: "Moves the contents of the internal RAM location
   addressed indirectly through register Ri to the direct address."
   Source = @Ri, destination = direct.

   Test: R0=0x30, IRAM[0x30]=0x88. MOV 0x40,@R0.
   Expected: IRAM[0x40]=0x88.
   Before fix: IRAM[0x40]=0x00, IRAM[0x30]=0x00 (data destroyed).

---
 opcodes.c | 8 +++++---
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/opcodes.c b/opcodes.c
index abc1234..def5678 100644
--- a/opcodes.c
+++ b/opcodes.c
@@ -843,9 +843,10 @@ static uint8_t mov_mem_indir_rx(struct em8051 *aCPU)
 {
-    uint8_t address_from = OPERAND1;
-    uint8_t address_to = INDIR_RX_ADDRESS;
-    uint8_t value = read_mem_indir(aCPU, address_from);
+    /* MOV direct,@Ri: read from @Ri, write to direct address */
+    uint8_t address_to = OPERAND1;       /* direct address */
+    uint8_t address_from = INDIR_RX_ADDRESS; /* @Ri */
+    uint8_t value = read_mem_indir(aCPU, address_from);
     write_mem(aCPU, address_to, value);
     PC += 2;
     return 1;
@@ -1334,7 +1335,8 @@ static uint8_t xchd_a_indir_rx(struct em8051 *aCPU)
 {
     uint8_t address = INDIR_RX_ADDRESS;
     uint8_t value = read_mem_indir(aCPU, address);
-    ACC = (ACC & 0xf0) | (value & 0x0f);
-    value = (value & 0xf0) | (ACC & 0x0f);
+    uint8_t old_acc_low = ACC & 0x0f;
+    ACC = (ACC & 0xf0) | (value & 0x0f);
+    value = (value & 0xf0) | old_acc_low;
     write_mem_indir(aCPU, address, value);
     PC++;
